# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project contains no student data. Class results live only in each
# teacher's own browser -- site/analyze/ never uploads a file -- and preflight
# aborts the deploy if any student-derived field reaches site/.
#
# If you ever find yourself adding a rule here to exclude student data,
# something has been put in the wrong folder. Move it instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Scoring-materials PDFs: ~10MB each, 12 of them, and every page is a scanned
# image. Nothing in the build reads them; tools/fetch_sources.py --scoring
# pulls them on demand for the Phase 4 exemplar harvest.
sources/scoring/

# EVERY Imagine Learning guide, per-unit and course alike. Two reasons, and the
# second is the one that matters:
#
#   Size -- the per-unit guides are ~22MB each, nine of them, 203MB in total,
#   and git never forgets a binary.
#
#   LICENSING -- these are Imagine Learning's copyrighted curriculum. The three
#   course guides were tracked until the repository was first pushed to GitHub,
#   at which point 101MB of licensed PDF went to a third party's servers. They
#   were purged from history and the remote was rebuilt; do not re-add them.
#
# Nothing in the published build reads them. The extractors do -- see
# provenance/imagine_guides.md for which scripts, what they produce, and the
# sha256 of the edition this project was built against -- but their output is
# committed, so a clone rebuilds the site without them. preflight skips the
# regenerability checks that need them and says so.
sources/ImagineIM_NY_?_?_TG_*.pdf
sources/ImagineIM_?_?_TG_*.pdf
sources/ImagineIM_NY_?__TCG_*.pdf
sources/ImagineIM_?_?_TG_CCSS_*.pdf

# Housekeeping
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
~$*

# npm packages for the test harness -- reinstall with: npm install
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Netlify CLI state
.netlify/

# Editor backups -- local working files, not part of the project history
provenance/backups/

# Lesson-level index derived from the per-unit teacher guides. It reproduces
# Imagine Learning's Student Task Statements verbatim, so it is kept out of the
# repository for the same reason the guides themselves are, and build/payload.py
# never reads it -- only short cited quotes reach the published site. Rebuild it
# with tools/extract_im_ms_lesson_detail.py.
data/im_ms_lessons_detail.json
